			<textBox refId="TXT_SEPPmail_Computer_Tooltips_EN_Plain">
				<label>Plain</label>
				<defaultValue>Suppresses any cryptographic action, provided this is the company's internal default. This may make sense if the recipient requests it. This may be due to problems when opening the e-mail on mobile devices. It is essential to check whether the content of the e-mail allows unencrypted sending! If necessary, the use of "encryption with read confirmation" - and thus the use of GINA technology - should be preferred, since this also works on mobile devices.</defaultValue>
